"""Kubernetes Live/Mock Adapter Contract Tests — Phase 13G-8.

Verifies that a CoreV1Api-compatible mock client can be injected into
KubernetesProviderAdapter, producing a RawProviderSnapshot that feeds
directly into KubernetesProviderNormalizer — the SAME path as fixture mode.

Flow:

    Mock CoreV1Api-compatible client
        ↓
    KubernetesProviderAdapter(client=mock)
        ↓
    RawProviderSnapshot
        ↓
    KubernetesProviderNormalizer
        ↓
    NormalizationResult (Canonical Domain Model)

Key principles:
    - sanitize_for_serialization() is used ONLY at the adapter boundary
    - Normalizer never sees K8s client objects
    - Same adapter → snapshot → normalizer path for fixture/mock/live
    - No Workload inference, no Accelerator inference
    - No mutation (read-only API calls only)
    - No persistence

Live tests are SKIPPED when credentials are unavailable.
"""
